From: Clay Warren
Subject: [PATCH] Reject negative PostScript levels before calling Cairo

Cairo 1.18.4 checks only the upper bound before indexing its level-string
array. With signed MSVC enums, negative levels can reach that array.
Validate the Python integer first so the existing ValueError contract
and upstream test also hold on Windows.

--- a/cairo/surface.c
+++ b/cairo/surface.c
@@ -1725,7 +1725,7 @@
 
   level = (cairo_ps_level_t)level_arg;
 
-  s = cairo_ps_level_to_string (level);
+  s = level_arg < 0 ? NULL : cairo_ps_level_to_string (level);
   if (s == NULL){
     PyErr_SetString(PyExc_ValueError, "level_to_string: "
 		    "invalid level argument");
